WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.660
Welcome to Grade 5 English, Unit 2: Exploring Space.

2
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:07.160
Welcome to Unit 2!

3
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:12.140
In this unit, you will explore the
exciting world of space and discovery.

4
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:19.460
You will read about how people study the stars, build
amazing projects, and work together to achieve great things.

5
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.920
Along the way, you will learn new
vocabulary, practise important grammar skills,

6
00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.660
and develop your writing and speaking abilities.

7
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:33.860
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

8
00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:42.620
By the end of this unit, you will be able to use and
understand 25 new vocabulary words related to systems, science,

9
00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:44.020
and social values.

10
00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:51.660
you will also identify and use indefinite pronouns
such as everyone, somebody, nothing, and anything.

11
00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:56.840
you will also read and understand an
informative passage about space exploration.

12
00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.580
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:08.000
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
independence, issue, empire, expose, glare, source.

14
00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:13.880
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.640
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:25.610
The reading sequence includes Exploring Space:
source text 1 and Exploring Space: source text 2.

17
00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:26.800
Read actively.

18
00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:31.780
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:35.800
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:40.240
The first language focus is What Are Indefinite Pronouns?.

21
00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:47.040
Indefinite pronouns are special words that we use when
we want to talk about people or things in a general way,

22
00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:48.600
without being specific.

23
00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:54.880
They are called 'indefinite' because they do not
point to a definite or particular person or thing.

24
00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:59.420
For example, instead of saying: Notice
the structure in the model examples,

25
00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:03.300
then apply it deliberately in
connected sentences and paragraphs.

26
00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:09.840
In speaking, you will complete Speaking
1: Astronaut Interview Role-Play.

27
00:02:10.333 --> 00:02:15.080
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

28
00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:18.980
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

29
00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:22.580
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

30
00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:24.440
You are ready to begin.

31
00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:31.000
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

32
00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.620
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

33
00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:39.400
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
